# src/apps/daemon/internal/foundation/trafficstats

## Purpose
Authoritative cumulative traffic accounting and rate sampling used by telemetry truth.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `foundation` (rank 0; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (3): `accounting.go`, `rate_sampler.go`, `rate_sampler_test.go`

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `trafficstats`.
- Notable exported surface: `AddDownloadBytes`, `AddUploadBytes`, `GetEvasionTrafficStats`, `NewRateSampler`, `RateSampler`, `Rates`, `ResetEvasionTrafficStats`.
- Daemon-local dependencies: none.
- Direct daemon callers: `internal/adapters/api`, `internal/runtime/mobilecore`, `internal/runtime/proxy`.

## Invariants
- Rates derive from authoritative cumulative counters; unknown measurements remain unknown.
- `foundation` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

## Navigation
- Read this file first, then direct child `.context` files before editing a deeper folder.
- Update this context when ownership, supported interfaces, or child-folder meaning changes; do not use it as a changelog.
